  "qualifications": [
    "The copy is best effort and flushed per line, not an fsynced accounting boundary (memory design v4 section 7).",
    "Every Gateway of a user shares the directory: each line is appended under one lock file, which serializes sequence, rollover, retention and cap decisions on what is on disk (Codex Checkpoint C pass 1, finding 1); two real Gateway processes are exercised.",
    "Clock skew (Codex Checkpoint C pass 3): a line goes to its UTC day's newest segment or a newer day's, never an older one, so a segment dated in the future by a clock that runs ahead stays selected until the date catches up; it is still rolled at 64 MiB, and every record keeps its own time."
  ],
